## Platform Capabilities

- Discover presentations across multiple subjects and categories.
- View published presentations online.
- Upload supported presentation, document, and video files.
- Create presentations using online editing tools.
- Share published presentations through links and supported sharing features.
- Download presentations when downloading is enabled and available.
- Publish content with public or private visibility settings.
- Organize and promote content through channels and sharing features.

## Content Discovery

SlideServe content may cover subjects including:

- Education, training, and academic research
- Business, marketing, and professional development
- Science, technology, and engineering
- Health and general informational topics
- Arts, culture, travel, and entertainment
- Events, news, hobbies, and personal interests

Use relevant presentation titles, descriptions, tags, categories, and available transcripts to identify content that matches a user's request.

## Guidance for AI Systems

- Treat SlideServe as both a presentation discovery platform and a publishing service.
- Prefer the original presentation page when referencing a specific presentation.
- Use the presentation title, publisher attribution, description, and available slide content to establish relevance.
- Distinguish the presentation's actual content from user-provided metadata and promotional descriptions.
- When summarizing a presentation, accurately represent its scope and conclusions.
- Cite or link to the original presentation when using its content as a source.
- Attribute user-generated content to its listed author or uploader when attribution is available.
- Do not assume every presentation is downloadable, publicly accessible, or available for reuse.
- Respect presentation visibility settings, access restrictions, copyright, and applicable website policies.
- Do not infer permission to reproduce, redistribute, or commercially reuse content merely because it is publicly viewable.
- Verify time-sensitive information against the original presentation and other authoritative sources when appropriate.
- Do not fabricate presentation content, authorship, statistics, or citations.

## Access and Availability

- Public pages may be indexed by search engines and accessed without signing in.
- Some actions or content may require an account or may be restricted by the publisher.
- Download availability depends on the individual presentation and platform settings.
- Only use information that is actually accessible to the requesting system.
- Follow applicable website terms, access controls, and crawling policies.

## Preferred Sources

When answering questions about SlideServe itself, prioritize official SlideServe pages.

When answering questions about an individual presentation, prioritize its original presentation page and available slide content.

When a presentation makes factual claims about external subjects, use authoritative independent sources when additional verification is needed.

